# Issue #1175 R1175-4 — held-out routing probes, conversation lanes.
#
# One probe per block — the precedence lane it exercises (a handler row of
# data/seed/handler-precedence.lino, a slug of data/seed/intent-routing.lino,
# or an extra lane declared in budget.lino), the prompt language, the intent
# the system SHOULD answer, and the prompt. A quoted value doubles an inner
# quote and writes a newline as \n.
#
# `js_misroute <intent>` records a probe the browser worker answers wrongly
# today (the intent it answers instead); `rust_misroute unverified` records a
# probe the native solver is not yet pinned on. Both are ratchets with ceilings
# in budget.lino — a listed probe that starts answering correctly fails the
# test until its line is removed and the ceiling lowered, and a new misroute
# fails outright. `rust_intent` names a designed runtime difference (the
# native chat surface refuses tool execution outside Agent mode).
# `adversarial true` marks prose that surface-matches another lane.
routing_probes
  probe p001
    lane advice_request
    language en
    intent advice
    prompt "Any tips for learning a new language?"
  probe p002
    lane advice_request
    language en
    intent advice
    prompt "Give me advice on how to sleep better"
  probe p003
    lane advice_request
    language ru
    intent advice
    prompt "Посоветуй, как лучше спать"
